LAST_SUCCESS=Task 41 (system fonts loader) device-verified 2026-05-26. Third cross-app dep installed alongside markdown + emoji; loaded via the same generic wart-host introspection wiring ("loader: dep fonts instantiated; wired 2 fn(s) across 1 interface(s) into consumer linker (generic)"). MarkdownCard's H1/H2/body now render in NotoSerif (FontFamily.Serif), code-block + inline code in DroidSansMono (FontFamily.Monospace). FontsCard reports "208 files, 175 distinct families on /system/fonts/" with rendered Serif + Monospace samples.
NOTES=Three orthogonal pieces shipped: (a) system-fonts/ Rust component (own repo, needs Codeberg create + push — list-all + load reading from /system-fonts/ preopen); (b) wart-host preopens /system/fonts at /system-fonts in both standalone.rs + run_once.rs; (c) host font resolution gains family_alias_paths in canvas_impl.rs + push_text_style override in paragraph_impl.rs that maps Compose's Linux-platform aliases ("Noto Serif" / "Noto Sans Mono" / etc.) to actual /system/fonts/Noto*.ttf paths. SKIKO BUG FIXED: TextStyle.kt's fontFamilies array setter now mirrors first element into the singular fontFamily string so Compose's `res.fontFamilies = resolved.aliases.toTypedArray()` actually reaches the WIT layer (was empty before). Required skiko republish + compose-*-wasi rebuild (~3 min skiko + ~3 min compose). wart-app: FontsImports.kt hand-written binding + FontsCard composable; MarkdownCard now sets fontFamily = FontFamily.Serif on RenderRuns + RenderHeading. wit/wart-app.wit gains 3rd import (war:fonts/loader@0.1.0).
